Bundled libraries
-----------------
* Python .............. PSF License (bundled with the frozen executable)
* wxPython ............ wxWindows Library Licence (LGPL-compatible)
* sherpa-onnx ......... Apache-2.0
* ONNX Runtime ........ MIT
* numpy ............... BSD-3-Clause
* FFmpeg (optional) ... LGPL-2.1/GPL (downloaded on demand by the user)

TTS engines shipped in the catalog (sherpa-onnx ONNX family)
-----------------------------------------------------------
* Piper ............... MIT (code); voices under their own licences
  (mostly MIT or Apache-2.0; check each voice on its model page)
* Kokoro-82M .......... Apache-2.0
* Kitten TTS .......... Apache-2.0
* VITS (zh-AISHELL3) .. Apache-2.0 (code); AISHELL3 data for non-commercial use
* Matcha-TTS .......... Apache-2.0 (code); model checkpoints CC-BY-4.0 unless
  the model page states otherwise
* MMS TTS (Meta) ...... CC-BY-NC-4.0 (non-commercial)
* SAPI5 voices ........ Provided by Windows/the voice vendor; each voice keeps
  its own EULA. Use only voices you are licensed to use.
* Windows Core voices . Provided by Windows; governed by the Microsoft Windows
  licence terms of your installation.

OmniVoice engines (k2-fsa)
--------------------------
* OmniVoice ........... Apache-2.0
  (https://github.com/k2-fsa/OmniVoice)
* OmniVoice Server .... Apache-2.0
  (https://github.com/maemreyo/omnivoice-server; uses the k2-fsa OmniVoice
  model under Apache-2.0)

Voice Lab clone engines (installed per engine into their own environments)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Pocket TTS (Kyutai) . Apache-2.0 (code); the pre-made voices carry their own
  licences, and cloned voices remain the responsibility of the user
  (https://github.com/kyutai-labs/pocket-tts)
* Bark (Suno AI) ...... MIT (code and model); generated audio is subject to
  Suno's acceptable-use policy (https://github.com/suno-ai/bark)
* F5-TTS .............. MIT (code); CC-BY-NC-4.0 (model weights) -
  NON-COMMERCIAL unless you have a separate permission for the weights
  (https://github.com/SWivid/F5-TTS)

Other Python packages pulled in by the engines (torch, torchaudio, soundfile,
scipy, transformers and friends) keep their own licences - BSD/MIT/Apache-2.0
family for all of them; the exact list is visible with "pip license" inside
each engine environment.

The AI Voice Studio application itself does not grant any licence over the
voices, models or audio produced with them; the user is responsible for
respecting each component's licence and for lawful use of generated audio.
